{#
    Offer countdown — merchant-placeable component (home + builder pages).
    One SDK component does the whole band: headline, copy, background, the
    ticking clock and the call to action — <falak-countdown> given a `theme`.

    | Variable              | Type    | Description                                  |
    | component.title       | string  | localized server-side                        |
    | component.description | ?string | localized server-side                        |
    | component.ends_at     | string  | "YYYY-MM-DD" or "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm", store time |
    | component.end_text    | ?string | shown once the moment passes                 |
    | component.image       | ?string | background image URL                         |
    | component.style       | string  | dark | light | primary                       |
    | component.show_button | bool    | whether the CTA is offered at all            |
    | component.button_text | ?string | CTA label, localized server-side             |
    | component.button_url  | ?string | CTA target                                   |
    | position              | int     |                                              |

    Customizer bindings — full rules in README, "Customizer annotations".
    Every field is an attribute of the component, so each binds with
    `attr:<name>`; the component re-renders itself as the merchant types.

    `show_button` is the exception, and the reason is worth knowing. A field's
    `conditions` only decide whether the CUSTOMIZER OFFERS it — hiding the two
    button fields from the panel. Nothing about that reaches the storefront, so
    without the `{% if %}` below the button kept rendering after the switch was
    turned off. Visibility in the editor and visibility on the page are two
    separate decisions, and a theme has to make the second one itself.

    It carries no `data-falak-bind` because toggling it adds and removes
    attributes rather than changing one, which the attribute binder cannot
    express — so the preview reloads on save instead of updating as you type.
#}
{#
    Absent means shown: a countdown placed before this switch existed has no
    `show_button` in its saved settings, and it should keep the button it
    already had rather than lose it silently on the next deploy.
#}
{% set show_button = component.show_button is defined ? component.show_button : true %}

<section class="block block--countdown" id="countdown-{{ position }}" {{ falak_section() }}>
    <div class="container">
        <falak-countdown date="{{ component.ends_at }}" end-of-day boxed labeled size="lg"
                         theme="{{ component.style|default('dark') }}"
                         title="{{ component.title }}"
                         description="{{ component.description }}"
                         image="{{ component.image }}"
                         end-text="{{ component.end_text }}"
                         {% if show_button %}button-text="{{ component.button_text }}"
                         button-href="{{ component.button_url }}"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-button-text="button_text"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-button-href="button_url"{% endif %}
                         data-falak-field="title" data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.title') }}" data-falak-bind="attr:title"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-description="description"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-date="ends_at"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-end-text="end_text"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-image="image"
                         data-falak-bind-attr-theme="style"></falak-countdown>
    </div>
</section>
